WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.887
On this slide, we are focusing on nested loops: a loop inside a loop.

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:09.747
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:15.722
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.722 --> 00:00:19.882
A nested loop runs an inner loop for every outer item.

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:26.457
It can model combinations, but it can also become expensive and hard to read as data grows.

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:33.427
In real analytics, this pattern can support thresholds, validation rules, category assignment, alerts,

00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:36.457
and repeated processing.

00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:42.245
The examples are intentionally small so you can trace the logic from the condition to the result.
